WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.800
The best local model is not universal.

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:06.675
Model choice should follow the task, the data sensitivity, the hardware available,

00:00:06.675 --> 00:00:09.575
the expected output format, and the level of review required.

00:00:09.575 --> 00:00:13.090
A model that is strong for brainstorming may not be the best choice for structured

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:13.850
extraction,

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:16.520
code assistance, or careful policy drafting.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:19.830
Hardware fit is central. Local model performance depends on available memory,

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:24.240
accelerator support where present, CPU speed, storage performance, and context length.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:28.915
If the model does not fit the machine well, the user experience may be slow, unstable,

00:00:28.915 --> 00:00:30.440
or too constrained for the workflow.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:34.515
Quantized models can make local use more practical by reducing memory needs.

00:00:34.515 --> 00:00:37.635
That tradeoff may change speed, output quality, or reasoning behavior.

00:00:37.635 --> 00:00:40.640
The right question is not whether quantization is good or bad.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:44.010
The question is whether the model configuration meets the workflow's quality and

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.595
reliability needs.

00:00:45.595 --> 00:00:49.370
Smaller models can be excellent for drafts, routing, simple transformations, study help,

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:50.680
and routine assistance.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:54.280
Larger models may help with deeper reasoning or more complex synthesis when the local

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:55.715
hardware supports them.

00:00:55.715 --> 00:00:58.045
Either way, the model should earn trust through testing.

00:00:58.045 --> 00:01:00.520
Evaluation should use the learner's own prompt sets.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:04.615
Try representative requests, compare outputs, note failures, and choose based on evidence.

00:01:04.615 --> 00:01:08.865
A local AI workflow is strongest when model selection is based on actual use,

00:01:08.865 --> 00:01:10.715
not reputation alone.

00:01:10.715 --> 00:01:14.390
Keep notes about why a model was accepted, rejected, or reserved for a narrow task.
